advapi32,shell32: Report the Windows user as "protium", not "crossover".

CrossOver Hack 12735 pins the Windows user name to "crossover" so that a
bottle's profile path is the same on every machine. crossover-sources-26.3.0
carries it in three places, all commented with that bug number: GetUserNameA
and GetUserNameW in dlls/advapi32/advapi.c, which short-circuit ahead of the
WINEUSERNAME lookup unless CX_REPORT_REAL_USERNAME is set in the environment,
and the %USERPROFILE% branch of _SHExpandEnvironmentStrings in
dlls/shell32/shellpath.c. A protium prefix built from nothing therefore has
its profile at C:\users\crossover and reports crossover from cmd's %USERNAME%.

The third site is the one that decides the directory name, and it is
independent of the other two. The profile path does not follow from
GetUserName, and it does not follow from the Unix user either: CSIDL_PROFILE
is a CSIDL_Type_User folder with no parent, so _SHGetDefaultValue returns the
literal "%USERPROFILE%", and _SHExpandEnvironmentStrings expands that by
appending its own hardcoded userName[] to the ProfilesDirectory prefix. The
name is spelled as a character array rather than a string literal, which is
why grepping the tree for "crossover" does not find it. wineboot reaches this
through SHGetFolderPathW( CSIDL_PROFILE ) and writes the answer to
USERPROFILE, HOMEPATH and HOMEDRIVE; it writes USERNAME from GetUserNameW
separately. Patching advapi32 alone would rename the reported user and leave
the directory at crossover.

Keeping the name hardcoded, rather than restoring upstream's GetUserNameW call
in shell32, is deliberate: the prefix layout stays the same on every machine
regardless of the Unix account, which is the property the CodeWeavers hack was
after and the one protium wants too. It also leaves shell32 independent of
CX_REPORT_REAL_USERNAME, so setting that variable moves %USERNAME% to the Unix
account while the profile directory stays C:\users\protium. That divergence is
inherited from CrossOver, which has it already; protium does not set the
variable.

Applies to crossover-sources-26.3.0 (wine-11.0), on top of 0001.

--- a/dlls/advapi32/advapi.c
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/advapi.c
@@ -51,8 +51,8 @@
     /* CrossOver Hack 12735: Use a consistent username */
     if (!getenv( "CX_REPORT_REAL_USERNAME" ))
     {
-        len = sizeof("crossover");
-        if ((ret = (len <= *size))) strcpy( name, "crossover" );
+        len = sizeof("protium");
+        if ((ret = (len <= *size))) strcpy( name, "protium" );
         else SetLastError( ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER );
         *size = len;
         return ret;
@@ -76,8 +76,8 @@
     /* CrossOver Hack 12735: Use a consistent username */
     if (!getenv( "CX_REPORT_REAL_USERNAME" ))
     {
-        len = ARRAY_SIZE( L"crossover" );
-        if ((ret = (len <= *size))) wcscpy( name, L"crossover" );
+        len = ARRAY_SIZE( L"protium" );
+        if ((ret = (len <= *size))) wcscpy( name, L"protium" );
         else SetLastError( ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER );
         *size = len;
         return ret;
--- a/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
@@ -2632,8 +2632,8 @@
         }
         else if (!wcsnicmp(szTemp, L"%USERPROFILE%", lstrlenW(L"%USERPROFILE%")))
         {
-            /* CrossOver Hack 12735 */
-            static const WCHAR userName[] = {'c','r','o','s','s','o','v','e','r',0};
+            /* CrossOver Hack 12735, with protium's name in place of theirs. */
+            static const WCHAR userName[] = {'p','r','o','t','i','u','m',0};
 
             lstrcpyW(szDest, szProfilesPrefix);
             PathAppendW(szDest, userName);
